# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# .gitattributes — MDT-OEM-Extensibility
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# This repository ships build tooling, per-vendor recipes, and small
# customization assets. It does NOT ship vendor installers, downloaded
# caches, or built .7z archives. The rules below group by concern:
#
#   1. Default behavior
#   2. Windows text files (CRLF)
#   3. Registry files (UTF-16 LE, CRLF)
#   4. Cross-platform text files (LF)
#   5. Binary files (defensive — no vendor binaries should be committed)
#   6. Linguist classification
#   7. Export-ignore rules
#
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. DEFAULT BEHAVIOR
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

* text=auto


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 2. WINDOWS TEXT FILES
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Files consumed by Windows tools that expect CRLF line endings.

*.ps1       text eol=crlf
*.psm1      text eol=crlf
*.psd1      text eol=crlf
*.ps1xml    text eol=crlf
*.cmd       text eol=crlf
*.bat       text eol=crlf
*.xml       text eol=crlf
*.inf       text eol=crlf
*.ini       text eol=crlf
*.txt       text eol=crlf


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 3. REGISTRY FILES
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .reg files must be UTF-16 LE with a BOM and CRLF. The working-tree-encoding
# attribute enforces the encoding on checkout.

*.reg       text eol=crlf working-tree-encoding=UTF-16LE-BOM


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 4. CROSS-PLATFORM TEXT FILES
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Files read by tools and editors on any platform. LF in the repository.

*.md        text eol=lf
*.json      text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.sh        text eol=lf
.gitattributes  text eol=lf
.gitignore      text eol=lf
.gitmodules     text eol=lf


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 5. BINARY FILES
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This repository should not contain vendor binaries. The rules below are
# defensive: if a contributor accidentally commits one, Git will not mangle
# it, and the reviewer will immediately notice the mistake.

# Executables and installers
*.exe        binary
*.com        binary
*.scr        binary
*.msi        binary
*.msp        binary
*.msu        binary
*.cab        binary
*.psf        binary
*.msix       binary
*.msixbundle binary
*.msixupload binary
*.appx       binary
*.appxbundle binary
*.appxupload binary

# Libraries and drivers
*.dll        binary
*.ocx        binary
*.cpl        binary
*.sys        binary
*.cat        binary
*.bin        binary
*.dat        binary
*.rom        binary
*.efi        binary

# Archives
*.zip        binary
*.rar        binary
*.7z         binary
*.7z.001     binary
*.7z.002     binary
*.7z.003     binary
*.7z.004     binary
*.7z.005     binary
*.7z.006     binary
*.7z.007     binary
*.7z.008     binary
*.7z.009     binary
*.7z.010     binary
*.tar        binary
*.tar.gz     binary
*.tgz        binary
*.gz         binary
*.bz2        binary
*.xz         binary

# Disk and OS images
*.iso        binary
*.wim        binary
*.esd        binary
*.swm        binary
*.vhd        binary
*.vhdx       binary
*.vmdk       binary
*.vdi        binary
*.ffu        binary

# Image assets — committed only as small customization assets
*.jpg        binary
*.jpeg       binary
*.png        binary
*.gif        binary
*.bmp        binary
*.ico        binary
*.tif        binary
*.tiff       binary
*.webp       binary
*.theme      text eol=crlf
*.themepack  binary
*.svg        text eol=lf

# Fonts
*.ttf        binary
*.otf        binary
*.woff       binary
*.woff2      binary

# Cryptographic material (should never be committed, but classify correctly)
*.pfx        binary
*.p12        binary
*.key        binary
*.pem        text eol=lf


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 6. LINGUIST CLASSIFICATION
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Tell GitHub Linguist how to count these files in repository stats.

# Documentation is not code
docs/**       linguist-documentation
.github/**    linguist-documentation
README.md     linguist-documentation
CHANGELOG.md  linguist-documentation
CONTRIBUTING.md  linguist-documentation
CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md  linguist-documentation

# Recipes are configuration data, not code
vendors/**/Recipe.json  linguist-documentation

# Schemas are configuration
schema/**   linguist-documentation


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 7. EXPORT-IGNORE RULES
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Developer-only files that do not belong in `git archive` output or
# GitHub's auto-generated source tarballs.

.github/          export-ignore
.gitattributes    export-ignore
.gitignore        export-ignore
tests/            export-ignore
CONTRIBUTING.md   export-ignore
CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md export-ignore
CHANGELOG.md      export-ignore


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# END OF .gitattributes
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# If you add a new file type to the repository, consider whether it needs
# an explicit rule here. The default `* text=auto` covers most cases, but
# Windows-specific and binary files benefit from being called out.
